      "How do we make sure it actually lands?",
      "Each step explained",
      "01",
      "Diagnose",
      "What are we actually trying to solve?",
      "Almost every AI request I get is a symptom of something else. \"We want a chatbot\" usually means first-line customer questions take too long to answer. So I never start with the requested solution, but with the outcome you want and the process that currently stands in the way of it.",
      "What we do",
      "Interviews with business, IT, data and the people doing the work",
      "Analysis of existing documents, pilots and vendor proposals",
      "Data scan of the sources relevant to the question",
      "Framing the outcomes in measurable terms",
      "What it delivers",
      "A problem statement the whole core group signs off on, with measurable outcomes.",
      "02",
      "Prioritize",
      "Which use cases earn money, time and attention?",
      "This is where the list gets shorter, not longer. Every candidate is assessed the same way: value, feasibility, data readiness, change burden, and whether there is an owner in the line who actually benefits. We score together, not in my spreadsheet.",
      "What we do",
      "Uniform scoring on value, feasibility, data and change burden",
      "First-pass value estimate with visible assumptions",
      "Ownership assigned per use case",
      "Explicit record of what drops out and why",
      "What it delivers",
      "A prioritized portfolio with owners, plus a documented drop list.",
      "03",
      "Decide",
      "Build, buy or partner, and why?",
      "A substantiated choice per theme. Build where it differentiates you, buy where it is a commodity, partner where you want to steer the outcome without owning the technology. Including the costs that only become visible in year three.",
      "What we do",
      "Build/buy/partner assessment per theme",
      "Order-of-magnitude TCO over three years",
      "Architecture and dependency consequences",
      "Risk classification and compliance implications",
      "What it delivers",
      "A decision document that clears procurement and the board without an extra round.",
      "04",
      "Ship & govern",
      "How do we make sure it actually lands?",
      "The phase where most initiatives stall. Who manages it, how do you measure whether it still works, what happens when it breaks, and who is allowed to stop it? We settle this before building, not after.",
      "What we do",
      "Operating model, roles and cadence",
      "Measurement setup with a baseline before the start",
      "Governance: register, gate, periodic review, escalation path",
      "Adoption approach per role instead of a single rollout",
      "What it delivers",
      "A working solution with management, measurement points and an owner who is accountable for it.",
      "What you can expect from me",
      "Independent, vendor-neutral advice",
      "Clear, decidable and without noise",
      "Focus on value: time, money and risk",
      "Pragmatic and executable within your organization",
      "Transparent communication and a fixed cadence",
      "Measurable results and an honest evaluation",
      "What I don't do",
      "No endless pilots without direction",
      "No tool-stacking without strategy",
      "No selling of software or licenses",
      "No vague stories without substantiation",
      "No taking over your responsibility",
      "No \"AI for the show\"",
      "Investment & models",
      "Defined assignmentFor scoped advice, workshops and second opinions. Fixed price per assignment, set out in the proposal.",
      "Fixed-scope projectClear scope, milestones and deliverables for a fixed price or range. Fast to results.",
      "RetainerOngoing steering and availability in a fractional role. Fixed monthly amount, fixed rhythm.",
      "We agree on a model together →",
      "Independence, made concrete",
      "Why I can advise \"don't buy.\"",
      "Independence is easy to claim and hard to verify. That's why it's listed below as a commitment, not a promise, and why it's also in the engagement confirmation.",
      "No software commissions",
      "No affiliate deals",
      "No vendor kickbacks",
      "No margin on implementation partners",
      "Conflicts of interest disclosed upfront",
      "Procurement",
      "Frequently asked questions from procurement.",
      "✓",
      "Independence",
      "100% vendor-neutral. My advice is based solely on your interest, and any interests are disclosed upfront.",
      "▣",
      "Data & security",
      "I work within your policies and process no data without a written agreement or data processing agreement.",
      "▤",
      "Contract & terms",
      "Clear agreement, terms tailored to you, and transparent IP arrangements: the work is yours.",
      "✓",
      "Compliance",
      "Experience with governance, risk, audit and reporting to the board and supervisory bodies.",
      "All frequently asked questions about working together, pricing and data →",
      "Ready for impact?",
      "Ready for clear AI decisions?",
      "Book a no-obligation call. No pitch. Just sharp questions.",
      "30 min., no pitch deckBook a call →"
    ]
